WEBVTT

00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.520
"Human"?

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:06.820
Shoebill, do you know what 
species of animal she is?

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:09.640
I think she might be a "human."

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:13.520
I've only heard rumors, so I 
don't know much about them.

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:16.460
But I hear that, like you, they 
come up with lots of strange ideas,

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:18.590
and they're supposed to be very clever.

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:19.990
A human...

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:23.070
What kind of animal is that?

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:25.710
What do they look like?
Do they have claws and fangs?

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:27.470
I don't know what they look like.

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:33.470
I just know that they're smart and know a lot, 
and can use and make different tools.

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:36.090
Does that ring any bells?

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:40.140
Not yet.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:43.920
Which Area do they live in? 
We'd like to go there.

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:48.440
Where do they live? Does anybody know?

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:52.790
No one knows?

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:57.900
Kaban-chan!

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:02.410
This is great! Now we only have 
to find out where "humans" live.

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:04.090
Yeah.

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:07.170
Maybe that's what you 
should ask at the library.

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:09.900
To get to the library, 
go into the Forest Area

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:12.510
and turn right at the 
second fork in the road.

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:14.260
Be careful where you turn.

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:15.010
Got it.

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:16.630
Thank you for your help.

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:20.150
Shoebill-chan, you were 
a big help, too. Thanks.

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:24.560
But why didn't you say what was on your 
mind sooner? We were pretty scared.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:30.310
I don't mean to, but I always end 
up staring when I see a chance.

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:34.360
Oh, okay. Here I thought you were mad at us.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:38.510
Sorry. I honestly want to chat
with everyone more cheerfully.

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:41.740
I know it's not cute when I stay too quiet...

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:43.010
You really are scary!

00:01:43.010 --> 00:01:44.410
Hey, that's mean!

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:46.440
See ya.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:48.330
Take care now.

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:52.580
That was a pretty hectic Area.

00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:56.130
I know. I never thought 
we'd end up in a battle.

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:58.530
But now we can get to the library!

00:01:58.530 --> 00:01:59.470
Yeah.

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:04.430
I wonder what kind of habitat 
you live in? I can't wait to see.

00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:09.390
Sorry in advance if it's a 
really dark or cold place.

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:12.690
I can see in the dark, so that's no big deal.

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:16.410
If it's cold, well, maybe 
I'll stop at the entrance.

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:18.110
Aww, that's mean!

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:57.180
There are so many trees.

00:03:57.180 --> 00:04:00.130
It's pretty how the sunlight 
filters through them.

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:14.790
What's this thing?

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:18.020
Maybe there's something to the right.

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:20.010
Wanna check it out, 
since we've stopped already?

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:21.440
Yeah, let's.

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:22.570
Understood.

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:25.660
It goes pretty far.

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:27.030
Let's go, let's go!

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:27.570
Okay.

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:32.020
Got them.

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:33.760
We got them.

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:37.250
It's all winding.

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:46.190
It's kind of like a room.

00:04:46.190 --> 00:04:48.300
Huh? I see something.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:59.360
<b>Question:
A camel can drink 500 cups of water at a time. 
If True: Proceed right. 
If False: Proceed left.</b>

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:50.830
What's this thing?

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:55.850
"A camel can drink 500 
cups of water at a time."

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:59.360
"If true, proceed right. 
If false, proceed left."

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:02.480
Huh? Kaban-chan, what are you saying?

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:04.840
Huh? That's what the writing says.

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:06.160
There's writing?

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:09.910
<b>Question:
A camel can drink 500 cups of water at a time. 
If True: Proceed right. 
If False: Proceed left.</b>

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:09.910
Yeah. This word says "question."

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:13.890
"Word"? Oh, so you call this a word?

00:05:13.890 --> 00:05:16.170
Kaban-chan, you really are amazing.

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:18.670
Y-You think so?

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:22.480
I bet that's true, because 
the desert is really hot.

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:26.470
Are we supposed to go in the 
direction of the correct answer?

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:28.200
Then we go right.

00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:31.310
Wait, Serval-chan!

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:36.810
<b>Correct! 
Camels drink 80 liters at a time, and can 
drink up to 136 liters of water. They can even 
drink water with high salt concentration.</b>

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:35.760
It says we were correct.

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:36.810
Awesome!

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:39.140
500 cups? Wow.

00:05:39.140 --> 00:05:42.650
I can understand how they feel. 
Your throat gets so dry in the desert.

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:47.100
This is the next question.

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:48.160
There's another one.

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:50.120
Let's see...

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:53.110
"The water is stored in the camel's hump.

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:56.210
<b>Question: 
The water is stored in the camel's hump. 
If True: Proceed right.
If False: Proceed left.</b>

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:56.210
If true, proceed right. If false, proceed left."

00:05:57.560 --> 00:05:59.980
So that's why they can drink so much water!

00:05:59.980 --> 00:06:02.310
Camels have humps?

00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:03.960
Yup! I've heard about that.

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:06.010
We go this way, then!

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:11.110
Huh?

00:06:11.110 --> 00:06:13.260
Isn't this...

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:18.640
<b>Question: 
A camel can drink 500 cups of water at a time. 
If True: Proceed right.
If False: Proceed left.</b>

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:16.410
Serval-chan, this is the first room.

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:18.640
Huh? But why?

00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:23.150
Maybe you end up back here if 
you choose the wrong answer.

00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:26.110
Meow! I won't lose!

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:27.380
One more time!

00:06:28.290 --> 00:06:30.810
Okay, this time, we'll go the other way.

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:39.540
<b>Correct! 
Camels storing water in their humps is a myth. 
Actually, a camel's hump stores fat. Concentrating 
their body fat in one place as humps 
helps keep their bodies from getting too hot.</b>

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:39.540
"Camels storing water in their 
humps is a myth. Actually..."

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:43.620
So the humps have nothing to do with that.

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:46.800
They actually help alleviate the heat, huh?

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:49.590
There's the next sign.

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:52.180
All right! Let's keep moving.

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:54.760
We were wrong?

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:56.240
We did it!

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:57.310
<b>Correct!</b>

00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:57.550
Go, us!

00:06:57.550 --> 00:06:59.060
Awesome!

00:06:57.560 --> 00:06:59.060
<b>Correct!</b>

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:00.890
We were wrong?

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:02.810
No good?

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:04.900
It's the other way around?

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:12.220
I feel like we've walked a whole lot.

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:13.840
You said it.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:17.390
Boss, can't you tell us the answer?

00:07:17.390 --> 00:07:20.160
Lucky-san isn't saying anything.

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:24.420
Because we're inside an attraction. 
Do your best to answer them.

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:27.580
All right! This is...

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:31.230
Which way do you think, Kaban-chan?

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:35.010
I think this one's true, maybe.

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:37.470
Okay! To the right!

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:47.830
It's bright and open here.

00:07:50.630 --> 00:07:52.430
Is that the library?

00:07:53.130 --> 00:07:54.410
It's incredible.

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:56.630
I see a big tree inside it.

00:07:56.630 --> 00:08:00.950
Is the professor in there? 
Let's go check it out!

00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:06.290
Serval-chan!

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:09.250
Huh? What happened?

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:12.690
Order: Strigiformes
Family: Strigidae
Genus: Ptilopsis

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:13.320
Good day. I am Professor 
Northern White-faced Owl.

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:16.090
Good day. I am her assistant, 
Eurasian Eagle Owl.

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:16.090
Order: Strigiformes
Family: Strigidae
Genus: Bubo

00:08:16.860 --> 00:08:18.740
Hello. I'm Kaban.

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:23.100
Where did you two come from? 
I didn't hear a thing!

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:26.730
For us, flying without making 
a sound is elementary.

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:29.840
You're the first Friends to make it this far.

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:31.940
We have high hopes for you.

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:34.980
We're the first? Awesome!

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:40.410
Huh? I thought lots of other Friends 
had come here to look things up.

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:44.870
If you take the road straight instead 
of the maze, you'd arrive over there.

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:47.670
Huh? What's with that?

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:52.090
The Friends who occasionally go in through 
the right generally get lost and leave.

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:53.570
We fell for it.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:57.510
They're promising, aren't they, Professor?

00:08:57.510 --> 00:09:02.020
Indeed, assistant. Today we will feast.

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:06.000
Anyway, we were hoping you could tell 
us what kind of animal Kaban-chan is.

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:08.480
At the library, you answer questions, right?

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:09.910
That's elementary.

00:09:09.910 --> 00:09:13.940
If you want us to answer your 
questions, you will cook for us.

00:09:14.250 --> 00:09:15.780
Cook?

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:20.000
Cooking means to combine 
ingredients in such a way as

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:23.040
to create food dishes of 
different shapes and flavors.

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:24.160
It does.

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:27.490
Why not just eat Japari buns? 
They're delicious.

00:09:27.490 --> 00:09:29.150
We're tired of eating them.

00:09:29.150 --> 00:09:30.760
It is true that Japari buns

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:35.530
have the perfect balance of 
nutrients and fill our stomachs...

00:09:35.530 --> 00:09:37.310
But we are food lovers.

00:09:37.310 --> 00:09:42.970
Since we have these bodies now, we wish to 
eat things we can only eat in these forms.

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:48.320
Besides, using our brains means using 
energy. And since we are wise...

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:54.180
If we have no food, we might not be able 
to remember. And since we are wise...

00:09:54.180 --> 00:09:55.610
Really?

00:09:55.610 --> 00:09:58.960
Now, try to satisfy our stomachs.

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:01.570
Will you do it or not?

00:10:01.570 --> 00:10:03.450
Sounds fun.

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:04.370
We'll do it!

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:05.750
Y-Yeah.

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:13.870
The distinctive long feathers over 
their eyes are called ear tufts.

00:10:06.390 --> 00:10:35.670
Tobu Zoo, Kidokoro-oneesan (Saitama)

00:10:13.870 --> 00:10:17.860
Owls like the Eurasian scops owl and the 
brown hawk-owl are relatively small,

00:10:17.860 --> 00:10:22.500
while horned owls are relatively large. 
That's one way owl species are divided up.

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:26.700
Compared to other birds of prey 
like hawks, they're slow fliers.

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:29.790
Their hunting style is to attack prey 
after the prey comes close.

00:10:29.790 --> 00:10:35.330
So I think of them as pretty 
laid-back for a bird of prey.

00:10:36.230 --> 00:10:41.550
Scops owls can squeeze their bodies to 
disguise themselves as tree branches.

00:10:36.420 --> 00:11:05.620
Ikefukurou Owl Café, Nakajima-oneesan (Tokyo)

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:45.490
They're gray in color, 
their plumage is glossy,

00:10:45.490 --> 00:10:48.010
and they have ear tufts over their eyes.

00:10:48.010 --> 00:10:50.820
It's cute how they have a 
mustache like an old man.

00:10:50.820 --> 00:10:52.550
They're pretty expressive.

00:10:52.550 --> 00:10:54.580
When they're annoyed,
they'll make an annoyed face,

00:10:54.580 --> 00:10:57.900
and when they find something 
interesting, their eyes will sparkle.

00:10:57.900 --> 00:11:02.360
Each individual owl has 
their own likes and dislikes.

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:05.810
It's pretty fun when you notice 
the differences between them.

00:11:17.850 --> 00:11:20.730
You may read about cooking here.

00:11:20.730 --> 00:11:25.970
Since you were able to pass through the 
Quiz Forest, you must be able to read.

00:11:25.970 --> 00:11:29.660
You should refer to the books and 
cook using the ingredients provided.

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:29.660
<b>Eggplant and Spring Onion Tomato Sauce Stew</b>

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:32.350
Your time begins now.

00:11:32.350 --> 00:11:33.290
Huh?

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:39.410
If you can prepare a dish we find 
tasty before this sand runs out,

00:11:39.410 --> 00:11:42.500
we'll tell you what kind of animal you are.

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:45.140
We'll also throw in a bonus prize.

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:47.040
Okay! I'm ready!

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:47.890
Yeah!

00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:50.630
Think you can understand it?

00:11:50.630 --> 00:11:55.040
Yeah. It says the dishes you can cook 
depend on the ingredients you have.

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:57.900
Then we should see what we 
have to work with first.

00:12:00.190 --> 00:12:02.060
That's a lot!

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:06.470
Where did you get these ingredients?

00:12:06.470 --> 00:12:09.720
We borrowed a teensy bit from 
the field where the ingredients

00:12:09.720 --> 00:12:11.040
for Japari buns are grown.

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:12.410
A teensy-weensy bit.

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:16.420
Can't you just eat them like this?

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:19.730
It is not cooking until the ingredients 
have been prepared somehow.

00:12:19.730 --> 00:12:24.590
We are not interested in unprepared food.

00:12:24.590 --> 00:12:28.010
That sounds like a lot of work. 
Why would you do that?

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:32.960
We have to use what we have here, 
and it has to be simple...

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:34.600
Maybe this one?

00:12:34.600 --> 00:12:35.730
Let me see!

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:40.800
Got it! What do we do first?

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:42.780
It says we start with...

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:47.190
She can read perfectly. She must be a human.

00:12:47.190 --> 00:12:52.810
If she is a human, she's sure to be 
able to cook a dish for us. Drool...

00:12:52.810 --> 00:12:57.350
Finally, we'll be able to 
taste cooking. Drool...

00:12:57.350 --> 00:12:59.840
Huh? Did you just say "human"?

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:03.460
I haven't the foggiest idea
what you're talking about.

00:13:03.460 --> 00:13:08.470
We might remember once we've 
eaten a dish. Get cooking.

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:12.680
Excuse me, but it says we 
need something called a pot?

00:13:12.680 --> 00:13:14.050
Glad you asked that.

00:13:14.050 --> 00:13:15.060
Come with us.

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:20.190
You can use this place.

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:24.750
The Lucky Beasts seem to maintain it 
occasionally, so it can be used.

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:27.360
What is all this?

00:13:29.710 --> 00:13:31.140
What do we do with this?

00:13:31.140 --> 00:13:36.220
It says to put ingredients and water 
inside the pot and heat it to a boil.

00:13:36.220 --> 00:13:37.620
Do we have a heat source?

00:13:37.620 --> 00:13:40.020
Another excellent question.

00:13:40.020 --> 00:13:41.050
Not bad.

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:45.050
We can't just hand over fire to you. 
You'll have to look into it yourselves.

00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:47.670
I'll do some research and 
consider the options.

00:13:47.670 --> 00:13:51.810
In the meantime, Serval-chan, 
can you chop these up?

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:57.310
Um... um...

00:13:58.760 --> 00:14:01.940
Meow meow meow!

00:14:02.310 --> 00:14:05.430
Not bad. You finally made yourself useful.

00:14:05.430 --> 00:14:06.920
You are the chopper.

00:14:06.920 --> 00:14:08.820
All right! I'll chop these all up!

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:16.550
All of these methods look kind of hard. 
You need tools or strength...

00:14:16.550 --> 00:14:19.250
Maybe this one that uses wood?

00:14:22.990 --> 00:14:25.770
Serval-chan, I'm back.

00:14:25.770 --> 00:14:27.010
Whoa!

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:29.850
You chopped up so much. Thanks.

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:34.810
Next, we put this all in the pot...

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:37.270
Add water...

00:14:37.270 --> 00:14:39.870
And now we heat it to a boil.

00:14:39.870 --> 00:14:41.840
Oh, yeah! Did you find some fire?

00:14:41.840 --> 00:14:44.060
Yes. You need fire.

00:14:44.060 --> 00:14:45.860
You must obtain it.

00:14:46.560 --> 00:14:49.400
I thought I'd try getting some like this.

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:54.280
We place the paper on the ground, 
in a place that gets good sunlight, and...

00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:59.160
It's sparkling.

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:09.090
Now we move the fire to wood scraps 
and gradually add bigger pieces.

00:15:12.440 --> 00:15:14.850
This should be a big enough fire to boil the...

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:16.390
Huh?

00:15:16.800 --> 00:15:20.010
What are you all doing over there?

00:15:20.010 --> 00:15:20.670
Well...

00:15:20.670 --> 00:15:22.040
It's just...

00:15:22.040 --> 00:15:23.690
It's kind of scary...

00:15:23.690 --> 00:15:28.490
On medium heat, first warm up the 
ingredients, and then add spices.

00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:31.660
Place the rice we prepared here.

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:36.360
Gradually increase the heat, 
and then simmer at the end.

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:41.410
Once it's done, put out the fire 
and set it aside for a bit to cool.

00:15:41.410 --> 00:15:44.630
Serve it up with the rice, and...

00:15:46.910 --> 00:15:48.330
It's ready!

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:54.210
Let us restate the rules.

00:15:54.210 --> 00:15:57.440
If either of us approves of 
your dish, you pass,

00:15:57.440 --> 00:16:00.140
and we'll tell you what 
kind of animal you are.

00:16:00.140 --> 00:16:00.910
Now then...

00:16:00.910 --> 00:16:02.310
It's time for the judging.

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:09.460
Then again, it looks quite frightful up close.

00:16:09.460 --> 00:16:11.480
Is it supposed to look like this?

00:16:11.480 --> 00:16:13.570
Yes, I think so.

00:16:17.290 --> 00:16:20.870
Oh, you're supposed to use 
those tools to eat it.

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:22.470
Because it's hot.

00:16:22.470 --> 00:16:25.190
Do you two really know all about cooking?

00:16:25.190 --> 00:16:26.860
O-Of course!

00:16:26.860 --> 00:16:29.500
We were testing you.

00:16:51.180 --> 00:16:52.190
Spicy!

00:16:52.190 --> 00:16:53.700
It's spicy!

00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:57.190
What is this? Is it safe to eat?

00:16:57.190 --> 00:16:58.790
Drink some water.

00:17:01.070 --> 00:17:02.660
This is no good.

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:04.080
No good at all.

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:07.420
We can't tell you what kind 
of animal you are for this.

00:17:07.420 --> 00:17:08.500
What?

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:09.890
You can't?

00:17:09.890 --> 00:17:12.710
But we worked so hard to make it! Come on!

00:17:12.710 --> 00:17:16.670
No. This isn't edible.

00:17:17.920 --> 00:17:22.090
No. You must keep trying 
until we're satisfied.

00:17:22.090 --> 00:17:25.570
Is this even food?

00:17:25.570 --> 00:17:28.150
How can it have such a strong taste?

00:17:29.670 --> 00:17:31.260
Hey, you're eating it!

00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:32.570
This is so...

00:17:33.710 --> 00:17:37.860
I don't know why... but I can't stop.

00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:39.370
It's addicting.

00:17:40.090 --> 00:17:43.290
So this is cooking!

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:53.760
You pass.

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:57.340
We'll tell you what you want 
to know, so give us seconds.

00:17:58.400 --> 00:18:01.810
So, your tummies are full now, right? Tell us!

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:03.250
Very well.

00:18:03.250 --> 00:18:04.970
You are...

00:18:13.010 --> 00:18:14.440
...a human!

00:18:17.900 --> 00:18:21.900
Okay. Then Shoebill-chan was right.

00:18:21.900 --> 00:18:22.660
Yeah.

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:24.880
They're not surprised.

00:18:24.880 --> 00:18:28.710
This is when everyone usually gets impressed.

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:31.550
Can you tell us more about humans?

00:18:31.550 --> 00:18:33.090
Very well.

00:18:33.090 --> 00:18:36.250
Their identifying characteristics: 
they are bipedal.

00:18:36.250 --> 00:18:40.370
They have a high capacity for 
communicating, learning, and more.

00:18:40.370 --> 00:18:45.880
They are diverse and difficult to describe 
succinctly. A very unusual species.

00:18:45.880 --> 00:18:48.450
They live in groups. 
They can move great distances.

00:18:48.450 --> 00:18:51.330
They can throw. They're relatively large.

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:53.370
They have many interesting characteristics,

00:18:53.370 --> 00:18:58.340
but we find their ability to make 
and use tools deeply fascinating.

00:18:58.340 --> 00:19:03.220
In fact, the relics here in the park 
were all built by humans.

00:19:03.220 --> 00:19:05.020
Wow.

00:19:05.020 --> 00:19:07.610
But they look a little like 
us Friends, don't they?

00:19:07.610 --> 00:19:08.890
That's a foregone conclusion.

00:19:08.890 --> 00:19:13.880
We Friends are animals who 
were transformed into humans.

00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:16.050
Do you feel like you know what you are now?

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:18.090
It hasn't really hit me yet.

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:21.230
This is great! Now that we know 
what kind of animal you are,

00:19:21.230 --> 00:19:23.580
all we have to do is go 
to where the humans live.

00:19:23.580 --> 00:19:26.850
Hey, Professor, where can you 
usually find humans in the park?

00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:29.540
There aren't any. Not anymore.

00:19:29.540 --> 00:19:32.530
The humans went extinct.

00:19:33.280 --> 00:19:34.660
Extinct?

00:19:36.190 --> 00:19:39.110
One day, they disappeared.

00:19:39.110 --> 00:19:40.320
Why?

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:43.540
Either they couldn't live here...

00:19:43.540 --> 00:19:48.580
...or they're still here, but 
somewhere we don't know about.

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:50.870
Then we need to find the place.

00:19:50.870 --> 00:19:54.730
Whatever the case, you should go to an Area 
with an environment suitable for humans.

00:19:54.730 --> 00:19:59.130
Living in an Area that isn't right 
for you will shorten your lifespan.

00:19:59.130 --> 00:20:02.090
And one more thing. Near the humans—

00:20:02.090 --> 00:20:05.890
Oh, yeah! You said you'd give us 
a bonus prize, right? What is it?

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:08.180
Concert tickets.

00:20:08.180 --> 00:20:12.370
PPP Comeback Concert tickets are hot items, 
and impossible to get just anywhere.

00:20:12.370 --> 00:20:14.900
These ones even get you 
VIP treatment and handshakes.

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:16.420
Also, this.

00:20:16.420 --> 00:20:19.570
PPP? And what's that?

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:23.800
Oh, wow! We get to see PPP?!

00:20:24.380 --> 00:20:27.710
Oh, they're something called idols, 
and I've heard they dance and sing,

00:20:27.710 --> 00:20:29.240
and they're supposed to be amazing.

00:20:29.240 --> 00:20:31.790
We can really have these?

00:20:31.790 --> 00:20:33.190
They were given to us

00:20:33.190 --> 00:20:35.820
as thanks for lending our intelligence 
to help with their management.

00:20:35.820 --> 00:20:41.130
But we aren't too keen on noisiness, 
so you can have them.

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:47.420
I'm glad we got to eat cooking 
for the first time.

00:20:47.420 --> 00:20:48.890
I feel so satisfied.

00:20:48.890 --> 00:20:52.390
Wait, then how did the other Friends 
get you to answer questions?

00:20:52.390 --> 00:20:54.820
We just answered them.

00:20:54.820 --> 00:20:55.730
Huh?!

00:20:55.730 --> 00:21:00.130
We made you cook because you read 
your way through the Quiz Forest.

00:21:00.130 --> 00:21:02.030
I'm stuffed.

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:03.010
Bye now!

00:21:03.010 --> 00:21:04.700
Thank you!

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:09.910
Kaban, you should know that Ceruleans 
used to often be found near humans.

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:12.050
Be careful on the road.

00:21:12.050 --> 00:21:12.760
Huh?!

00:21:12.760 --> 00:21:15.000
No worries! I'll take care of them.

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:17.450
Serval's jokes aside...

00:21:17.450 --> 00:21:18.500
I'm not joking!

00:21:18.500 --> 00:21:21.590
If you see any, run away immediately.

00:21:21.590 --> 00:21:25.030
A good life comes from eating good food.

00:21:25.030 --> 00:21:28.970
Also, once you locate the humans, 
be sure to come visit again.

00:21:28.970 --> 00:21:31.760
We'll be waiting for seconds.

00:21:32.270 --> 00:21:33.150
You got it!

00:23:04.020 --> 00:23:06.890
This really is a lovely home.

00:23:06.890 --> 00:23:10.110
If you'd like, you should stay the night.

00:23:10.110 --> 00:23:12.450
I want to hear what happened next!

00:23:12.450 --> 00:23:17.970
Then, when I found the hat 
in the savanna—listen to this—

00:23:17.970 --> 00:23:20.080
Boss started talking!

00:23:20.880 --> 00:23:24.630
I saw Boss talking, too.

00:23:24.630 --> 00:23:25.820
What?!

00:23:25.820 --> 00:23:28.460
What did he say to you, Raccoon-san?

00:23:28.460 --> 00:23:31.280
Um, what was it again, Fennec?

00:23:31.280 --> 00:23:39.200
He said that something important 
to the Friends and us is underground.

00:23:39.200 --> 00:23:41.440
And as for where...

00:23:41.880 --> 00:23:43.220
PPP Preview!

00:23:43.220 --> 00:23:45.130
This week we're learning about the margay.

00:23:45.130 --> 00:23:47.040
They imitate the calls of other animals.

00:23:47.040 --> 00:23:48.720
Really? Wow!

00:23:47.640 --> 00:23:48.720
They imitate?

00:23:48.720 --> 00:23:49.740
Okay, Gen, you're up.

00:23:49.740 --> 00:23:50.690
Go ahead.

00:23:50.690 --> 00:23:52.570
Imitation of a margay.

00:23:53.670 --> 00:23:54.580
That's your guess?

00:23:54.580 --> 00:23:56.410
Next time: "PPP Live."
